{{smaller|'''Call for trumps''', in ''whist-playing'', a conventional signal indicating that the player wishes his partner to lead trumps. See ''peter''<sup>2</sup>, ''n.'' and ''v.''—'''To put to one’s trump''' or '''trumps''', to reduce to the last expedient, or to call for the utmost exertion of power: a figure borrowed from games at cards.}}

